problem-539.c:161:0:high:Flawfinder printf: If format strings can be influenced by an attacker, they can be exploited (CWE-134). Use a constant for the format specification. (risk 4, format)
problem-539.c:134:0:medium:Flawfinder char: Statically-sized arrays can be improperly restricted, leading to potential overflows or other issues (CWE-119!/CWE-120). Perform bounds checking, use functions that limit length, or ensure that the size is larger than the maximum possible length. (risk 2, buffer)
